  "stem": "A particle of mass ‘m’ moves along a circle of constant radius R with radial acceleration changing with time as $a_{r} = kt^{n}$ where k is a constant and n > 1. What is the power required for this motion as a function of time?",
  "options": {
    "A": "$\\frac{1}{2}mnRkt^{n - 1}$",
    "B": "$\\frac{1}{2k}mnRt^{n - 1}$",
    "C": "$\\frac{1}{k}mnRkt^{n - 1}$",
    "D": "$mnRkt^{n - 1}$"
  },
  "answer": {
